          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dc9890fbc96e5fe3586ff8ca3df6b95b4c6be855d82261424d5d5e9c3775e3e6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a86e1c81ae964edcbb28d2414b349c9d",
      "statement": "Resumption level 1 is the surviving workspace: `pipeline._fetch` returns immediately with the log line `repository workspace already present; resuming the generation` when `repo_dir/.git` exists, so a new claim with a fresh `claim_id` continues in `<DATA_DIR>/jobs/<wiki_id>/repo` without re-cloning; only a missing `.git` triggers a fresh fetch (after deleting any leftover non-git directory).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/services/pipeline.py#L155-L175",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1d18021511f3d91e26e4755eb93242627d29f42d60c5ae3c575444e175a2c511:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_69e2eeb1cef14319ad2e731061e29a44",
      "statement": "For a git source the retry/resume path needs nothing re-sent because the token is persisted in the `source` JSON column, while an upload source is only resumable while its archive still exists at `<job_dir>/upload<ext>`; otherwise `_fetch` raises `IngestionError(\"the uploaded archive is no longer available; submit the wiki again\")` and the wiki can only be fixed by re-submitting the archive.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/routers/wikis.py#L117-L135",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bbc9c1b8c0f737b70bfe80e97967f52732ab496b2e3ebe0da0ea14c03ade1271:"
