    {
      "id": "claim_316508ac25b743109b00764c23b87b22",
      "statement": "`tests/test_worker_queue.py` is the store-level specification of these semantics: `test_stale_claims_are_requeued` (a fresh claim untouched by `recover_stale(180)`, an old `last_seen_at` requeued with `claim_id is None` and `attempts` preserved), `test_complete_with_stale_claim_is_ignored` (wrong `claim_id` returns `False` and the row stays `fetching`), `test_heartbeat_cancel_and_complete` (heartbeat result shape and `cancel is True` after `cancel` returns `\"cancelling\"`) and `test_queued_cancel_and_retry` (immediate cancel and requeue of a never-claimed row).",
