    {
      "id": "claim_9da186a21b654af0b301ec5dc32d36d6",
      "statement": "`tests/test_api_wikis.py` exercises the recovery flows end to end with the fake CLI: `test_cancel_running_wiki_and_retry_resumes` (a slow generation reaches `generating`, cancel returns `cancelling`, the row becomes `cancelled` with `cancelled` in `error`, and retry ends `done`), `test_cancel_queued_wiki` (a wiki queued behind a busy worker is cancelled immediately as `cancelled`, not `cancelling`), `test_failed_wiki_can_be_retried`, `test_cancel_and_retry_validation` (`409`/`404`), and `test_active_wikis_are_resumed_after_a_restart`, which forces a running row with `claimed_by=\"crashed-worker\"`, `claim_id=\"deadbeef\"`, `last_seen_at=None` and no `wiki.zip` and relies on the startup `recover_stale` of a second `create_app` instance to requeue it until `done`.",
