    {
      "id": "claim_9ca3c8491a7441e5ba17b5c7f230448e",
      "statement": "The `failed` branches of `WorkerLoop._run` truncate their message to 500 characters (`error=str(exc)[:500]`) while the `PipelineCancelled` branch stores `str(exc)` untruncated, so a lease loss or a user cancel surfaces in the row as the readable message `the worker lease was lost` / `cancelled by user` rather than a traceback, and knowing which terminal branch truncates is what makes the `error` column useful for triage.",
      "evidence": [
